If you are a user of this social network you will know that from time to time new terms appear through expressions, popular hashtag and fashion terms.
Here you will find the most basic Instagram vocabulary, the most used terms, fashion hashtags yall instagram filtersExplained one by one.
Publications: all the photos and videos that you upload to the social network.
Influencers: users who have many followers with some credibility that cause a lot of interaction with their publications.
Comments: part of text that we write under the caption of a publication.
Explore: search function that allows you find other users on Instagram (profiles).
#hashtag instagram: is a content thematic grouping tag to identify a content.
Users can search for specific hashtags to find thematic content of it.
Direct: It is a function that allows you to send photos privately to one or more users. In this guide I explain in detail what is Instagram direct and how it is used
The expression in English means Throwback thursday and encourages the publication of childhood photos, personal historical moments and everything related to the past. Here you can see the detail What does the hashtag #tbt mean
It is the acronym for the English expression "Woman Crush Wednesday”And is used on Wednesdays. Users share photos of women who admire, from a mother, cousin, actress, singer, grandmother to a big screen heroine.
With more than 130 Millions of posts this tag is very popular and users use it frequently. It means "Follow for follow"And literally means" follow me and I follow you ", Internet users use it to get followers on Instagram fast and free instantly.
In English it means "Laughing my ass off ” and a rough vulgar translation would be "splitting my eyelet" or "dying of laughter".
With 9 millions of publications this hashtag is used to take selfies on Sundays. Users take pictures of themselves and upload them with this tag, although today it is already used regardless of whether it is Sunday or any other day of the week.
In English it means "Photo of the Day" and users use it to publish their best photo of the day.
It is not what it seems, this term literally translates as "an irresistible and appetizing meal" upon seeing it. You can already imagine what kind of 129 millions of photos that group this famous label, I invite you to take a look.
This term has a functionality similar to the one described above. #POTD and its translation is “Gram of the day”, Which is also the best publication of the day.
With more than 188 millions of photos tagged this expression is used to express your mood. Users upload an "expressive" video or photo along with a description explaining their status.
This hashtag already has 135 millions of posts, and in English it means “Outfit of the Day”. The translation would be "daily clothes" and it is widely used in accounts of bloggers, influencers and people who like fashion.
#GF This hashtag was created by a large community of instagramers who decided to support and teach the most beautiful photographic compositions worldwide.
Si quieres use Instagram Stories You can use many of these elements to create compositions that reach more users and impact the audience.
Apart from the labels that I have named, there are others that are trending and do not stop growing, that is, they are not as stationary as others that gradually stop being used.
In fact, one of the most famous that will happen to posterity, is the one that was made in the Oscar gala of 2014. Twitter had already been shared more than 1 a million times only 50 minutes after it was published.
It looks like the previous terms and consists of taking a picture of your hairstyle and hair. It has also been admitted to the Oxford dictionary and many actresses and models support and encourage such publications.
It's about uploading photos in bikini, less or more suggestive, but showing the space that is created between the hip. In fact, the literal translation is "bikini bridge."
The singer Beyoncé also contributed her photo participating in this phenomenon that has also lost relevance on Instagram.
The literal translation is "After the act" and on that it is based, upload photos after having done the act, although if you explore the channel where the term appears you will find everything.
These types of fashion hashtags can be dangerous as new actions and behaviors appear every day that can be grouped into a channel. As you have seen there are more normal and respectful and also more suggestive, becoming classified as adult content.
Once you select a photo to publish Instagram suggests 24 filters (it may vary because they are removing and incorporating new ones) to retouch your compositions before publishing them.
You may also be interested in other programs online photo filters very similar to Instagram with many options to retouch your photos
Tip: if you want to create a vintage-style photograph (postcard type) it also works great.
Clarendon is the most used filter by all Instagram users in the world, it is capable of improving the photos of any subject.
The cream filter is used more in outdoor photos creating a warm / cold effect making the image smooth and creamy.
The Hefe filter creates golden and yellow tones, even if the photo is a bit out of focus. It is often used to enhance vibrant colors in photos where there is diversity of color, for example, in a pool, flowers and landscapes with many elements.
The Hudson filter adds an extra cold and extra texture to the photo, highlights the contrast and shadows of your photography. If you try to apply the filter in pool or beach photos you will see how it creates a cold, icy and stiff effect on the image.
That is, yellow, orange and red colors intensify in photography. It is widely used both in selfies and landscapes.
The Ludwig filter increases the lighting of the photo and gently turns off the colors. It is recommended to use it for architecture, minimalist images, portraits and geometric shapes.
The Moon filter is like the Gingham, but in its black and white version, the final result is an image that has fragile lighting.
The Mayfair filter has a pink touch and seems to create an effect on the image as if it were 50 years. Appeared through an apology by the Instagram team.
The Nashville filter generates a warm and pleasant touch in your photos. It has a semi pink whole that further enhances the effect.
The Perpetual filter increases the yellow, green and blue tones of the photo, as if it were an image in full nature. It is great to use it for photos abroad, if you try it on the beach the effect is even more noticeable.
The Reyes filter desaturates each color creating a warm vintage effect with extra lighting. It is widely used for retro and old photos.
The Rise filter provides a reflection in the photograph and a soft illumination in the center, softening each faction and converting the colors to creams and yellows. It is as if the first light of day struck the photo with a warm glow.
It is widely used in landscape photos, outdoors and to create a relaxing and tranquil effect.
As the name implies (hibernate or sleep) the slumber filter desaturates the colors and creates a blurry effect. It would be something like a dream effect, retro or even melancholic.
The Valencia filter illuminates the picture with warm and bright colors. These warm tones make the image have a vintage and old effect (type 80 years), the photos seem washed out, but retain the original quality.
Also very useful for an improvised selfie without becoming a pure black and white, this filter enhances the colors with a spectacular effect.
The X Pro II filter intensifies many colors in the photo creating a warm and vibrant effect. It seems as if the photos were more lively and animated.
As new Instagram filters appear, I will update in this section.
Where to use small letters above for nick
