That is why with this Instagram dictionary you will understand what each of the expressions that are mentioned daily means in this great platform of photos and videos. Surely it has ever happened to you that you did not understand a certain publication or trending topic, now you will solve all your doubts.
Followers (Followers): Users who follow your activity (publications) and see your activity on the network.
Likes: interaction system to show your interest or pleasure in publications.
For example, when you put #dog you indicate that the photo or video belongs to that group, when other users also use the same tag, the content is grouped around the hashtag.
Filters: without a doubt the most popular function of the platform, they serve to retouch and edit the photos before publishing them. You have 23 filters, in addition to frames and other amazing effects.
This term is very famous since more than 1 Million photos have been tagged with this hashtag. Users use it to upload old photos from the past and are usually used on Thursdays of each week.
As you probably guessed, this tag is used in content that is funny and fun. Many of these publications end up becoming viral phenomena, so users tag their friends with #LMAO to make them laugh.
As its own name indicates Petstagram is used to label pets. Do a search for this popular hashtag and you will see more than 27 millions of videos and photos of cats, dogs, a hamster and rabbits.
They were also known as “Global family”They even had a website of their own, but now it is not as valid and all types of people use it to upload their photo of the day.
It is used to tag posts from people in the gym, weight loss, healthy habits, healthy food and anything related to fitness. There are more than 45 millions of tagged photos and it keeps increasing every day.
In English it comes to say "Shake My Head" and the translation means "going crazy" (shake my head). It is used when the publication is shocking, ridiculous or something that cannot be explained.
It fulfills the same function as #F4F and means “Like by like”, that is, an exchange of social interactions to get more likes in your post. It also enjoys a lot of popularity with more than 130 millions of uploaded images.
El meaning of LoLIt may vary depending on the context. It can be the famous RPG game (League of Legends) or the English expression of laughing out loud.
It comes from the English expression “Man Crush Monday” and it's the same as the tag #wcw but with men, although if you take a look you will realize that more photos of women are uploaded than men.
These letters in English mean "Black and White" (Black and white), so users upload photographs with black and white filters by grouping them with this label.
Now it has become fashionable to upload photos without filters. For this, this trend has been created where users through this hashtag post their photos without applying any type of filter that comes by default with Instagram.
This hashtag is not as popular (240k uploaded photos) but I wanted to name it. It means “Weekend Hashtag Project” and it is a contest that Instagram prepared some time ago every weekend where he invited users to upload beautiful photos.
By now you will know what it means, take a picture with your mobile or Tablet yourself. In the social network there are more than 310 millions of users who publish their selfies.
As curious facts, word of the year in 2013 was chosen by the Oxford dictionary and from that moment the mobile companies improved the resolution of the front cameras, in addition to incorporating the flash and multiple accessories.
This term started strong, but it seems that he has had many problems in the social network. It's about uploading pictures of the butt, buttocks and showing the back.
For example, Jessica Alba is a fan of taking photos of her hair, so the term gets more relevance.
This hashtag is used when taking group photos, although it can easily be confused with #selfie.
It is not as famous, but it was also used for a short period of time. Users upload photos of themselves drunk, but logically celebrities do not support these terms that they end up using, in addition to the embarrassing photos they can upload.
He had his fame, but little by little he has stopped using, they are the passing fashions of hashtags. It is true that in the summer time it regains some strength among users.
It had a negative impact since it can suggest the thinness of the woman and could create social alarm representing a beautiful body linked to weight loss.
As the name implies it is about taking pictures as soon as you wake up from the bed, although they have to be as natural as possible.
I name this one because I find it very curious and because new terminologies have been adapted based on this concept. It is about hanging photos with the rear air in any scenario, it is also used #buttsofinstagram o #cheekyexploits with the same objective.
In this video you can see all the Instagram filters, although if you want to know the detailed characteristics of each filter and for what situation each one is used, read on:
I will take this reference photo, these are the original images without any filter applied. I have used one of a building and another of a landscape with a person, so you can better see the differences of each of them:
This filter is perfect for portraits and stands out more when the colors are pastel. It provides a purple and pink tone to improve skin tone creating a more life effect in portrait photography.
If you have a photo that is a bit dark, the Amaro filter is perfect to apply. Increase the exposure of the photograph by illuminating the center of the photo and adding a bluish tone, on the contrary, it loses some contrast.
It is so famous because it brings a lot of brightness to the image, highlights the main elements and enhances all the blue tones of the photograph and the shadows.
It is used more for photographs of modern elements, architecture, cars and also photos taken abroad.
Inkwell is a filter of strong contrast and black and white. It can be used for photos with poor lighting and hide shadows, create an old effect or if the Willow filter does not work for you.
Juno is a filter widely used by instagramers, in fact, it is considered the most popular 2º in the world. It moderates the blue and green colors, enhances the intermediate and red tones, and changes the cold tone to a bright green.
The saw filter blurs the images a little by adding lighting in the center and forms a vignette in each corner. Apply yellow tones creating a warm effect on the photo.
It is often used in photos with pastel tones and delicate colors, sure to improve them.
The willow filter creates a gray color scale (black and white) but black colors are more like gray and white is a cream color. It is used for vehicles, furniture, faces, nature, architecture, landscapes and in the city.
It can be used perfectly in indoor, outdoor photos, to highlight colors and quality portraits.
