One of the most frequent concerns of users of Instagram and other social networks is the power know who visits your profile.
Obviously notifications do not let you know if that person has been looking at your profile, but that he likes a certain photo or has started to follow you.
But what about those users who pass silently?
Do those applications that promise to explain work?how to know who visits my Instagram"?
The truth is that "formally" It is not possible to know who visits your profile, the programs and apps that claim to know Instagram visits, really just looking to add you to their databases to make you look advertising and who knows what purposes.
2 Pages and applications that you should NOT download to try to know who visits your profile on Instagram
3.1 Are there alternatives on the internet?
However, the function Stories It's different, I've already told you in other posts of how to use Instagram stories and its strategic possibilities at the level <strong>Training</strong> business.
This way you can know "who visits my profile" in a matter of seconds.
It is perfectly possible to think that whoever visited your stories would also take a tour of your profile.
If you take the time to verify who makes up the audience of your stories, you will be able to know who your fans are, who only enters from time to time may not be interested, but those users who are attentive to your publications and constantly check your stories, they will surely do the same with your profile.
Among the possibilities offered to those who decide to use their services are:
You will know if a user has blocked you or has stopped following you
See the private photos of your contacts
As you can see, they offer functions and features that Instagram doesn't have, and also for free.
Also, reviewing in impartial forums (not web pages created to say if it works) I have verified that the option “who sees my Instagram profile” does not work.
It turned out to be so fraudulent which has already been removed from the App Store, its creator Turker Bayram, a famous malware developer, also managed to place the following application that already has problems with Google:
This app, similar to the previous one, was developed for users of devices with system Android on Google Play, such as Instacare and other fraudulent applications.
It also promised to be an application to see who visits your profile, but it turned out not to be like that.
It's another one of these free apps for iOS and Android, in which users eager for know who visits your profile they have been victims of unscrupulous developers.
Subsequently, and according to user complaints, the information was used to publish unauthorized photos of people, inappropriate and send spam on the social network of the colorful little camera.
All these apps have already been removed, but like Turker Bayram, other developers are constantly creating new applications that offer to fill you with followers, likes, such as knowing who looks at your instagram profile, keeping track of your posts, when what they really pursue is appropriate your data.
What to do if you have already installed one of these applications on your device?
You have had difficulty logging into your Instagram account
Try to enter Instagram with the last password you used and if you can't ask them to send you a link to recuperación password to your associated email account and change password.
To change your password, click on the avatar icon and select “edit profile", then "change Password”, Write the one you've been using so far and then a new one, confirm and you're done.
