So in an action of apparent "if you can't against them, join them" they have developed the Stories mode on Instagram, which, similar to the network of the yellow ghost, allows us share photos y videos that will have an ephemeral visibility in the network of 24 hours, time after which they will disappear.
Stories are not listed on our main Instagram wall and at the moment this feature does not support comments, although you can receive private messages. One of its peculiarities is that it keeps the record of who your stories, so you can know who is stalking you.
To access Stories, just click on the icon top with your avatar, there will be gathering the videos and photos uploaded during the last 24 hours and in the same chronological order they will leave fading.
The first time you encounter the new feature, in the first profile below the Instagram logo, from left to right in the screen on your mobile, you will find the Instagram camera, with the word new!
