News - What does the improvement of the fineness of the UV printer depend on?
Many UV printer manufacturers are also conducting tireless research on how to further improve the fineness of inkjet printing. UV inkjet printing is a subtractive process for the three primary colors of cyan (C) magenta (M) and yellow (Y).
From the perspective of the development trend of inkjet print heads, the size of the nozzle is getting smaller, the number of picoliters of the smallest ink droplet is decreasing, and the resolution is increasing. Now on the market such as Ricoh, Epson, Konica and other mainstream print heads, the smallest ink droplets are several picoliters.
Finally, spot colors are also a solution to further improve the fineness of UV printers. The color of other colors presented by the mixture of the three primary colors is still not as bright as the direct use of this color ink, so complementary color inks such as green, blue, orange, purple and other spot color inks have appeared in the market.
