Cause of failure: The nozzle is in poor condition. Solution: The nozzle is blocked or obliquely sprayed, and the nozzle can be cleaned;
Cause of failure: The distance between the nozzle and the printed matter is too far. Solution: Make the printed matter close to the print head and keep a distance of about 2 mm;
Cause of failure: ink precipitation or ink breakage. Solution: Check the status of the print head, whether the ink fluency has deteriorated, and check whether the ink path is leaking;
Cause of failure: The grating strip is dirty. Solution: clean the grating strip;
c. Cause of failure: poor contact or failure of the square-headed optical fiber cable. Solution: Replace the square fiber cable.
