The high pressure roller mill is very similar in form to the traditional double roller crusher, but there are two differences in essence.
In the process of using this machine for ore processing, the wet tail throwing of coarse-grained closed-circuit roller milling is a common process. The following figure shows the main process flow:
In the specific application of this process, the abrasive cake is mainly screened through a closed circuit, so that the particle size of the product processed by the high-pressure roller mill can always be controlled within a range that is very suitable for sorting and tailing, and finally achieve the purpose of pre-throwing the tail.
At the same time, in the process of using high-pressure roller mill for ore beneficiation and ore crushing production, under the action of side material effect, there will be a small part of ore particles with excessive particle size inside the extrusion cake. If this part is directly used During the grinding or beneficiation operation, the corresponding work flow will fluctuate greatly, which will bring a certain degree of adverse impact on the beneficiation production.
