The optical port of the switch is generally inserted into the optical module and connected to the optical fiber for transmission; some users will insert the electrical port module into the optical port and connect the copper cable for data transmission when the electrical port of the switch is insufficient. At present, the common types of switch optical ports are 155M, 1.25G, 10G, 25G, 40G and 100G, etc.
The transmission rate of common optical ports can reach more than 100G, and the maximum rate of commonly used electrical ports is only 10G;
The farthest transmission distance when the optical port is inserted into the optical module can be more than 100KM, and the farthest transmission distance when the electrical port is connected to the network cable is about 100 meters;
