Connect an adjustable attenuator and a PON optical power meter in series between the leather cable and the ONU, so that the PON optical power meter can be used to measure the received optical power of the ONU (the downstream optical power of the test). The difference between the received optical power of the ONU is about 0.3dB (1 fiber jumper minus the attenuation of an active connection).
For example, the ONUs in this test can still work normally when the receiving optical power is higher than -27.98dBm. When the received optical power is lower than -27.98dBm, the downlink network speed drops rapidly with the decrease of the received optical power, and maintains a very low network speed within a certain optical power range until the network is completely interrupted.
5G communication is actually the abbreviation of 5th Generation mobile networks, which mainly refers to cellular mobile communication technology. And our 5G here refers to the 5GHz in the WiFi standard, which refers to the WiFi signal that uses the 5GHz frequency band to transmit data.
However, 5GHz Wi-Fi also has shortcomings. Its shortcomings lie in the transmission distance and the ability to traverse obstacles.
Go around obstacles. Therefore, the 5G signal with high frequency and short wavelength has a relatively small coverage area, and the ability to pass through obstacles is not as good as 2.4GHz.
However, without these limitations, 5 GHz is a faster option. When we combine the advantages and disadvantages of these two frequency bands and combine them into one, by using dual-band access points in wireless deployment, we can double the wireless bandwidth, reduce the impact of interference, and enjoy all-round A better Wi-Fi network.
In the design of optical fiber network structure, many projects adopt the method of optical fiber transceiver + optical module connection. So, what do we need to pay attention to when connecting and purchasing products for optical fiber networks in this way?
The speed of the optical fiber transceiver and the optical module must be the same, for example, the gigabit transceiver corresponds to the 1.25G optical module
The wavelength and transmission distance must be consistent, for example, the wavelength of 1310nm is used, and the transmission distance is 10KM
Attention should be paid to the selection of fiber jumper pigtail interface. Generally, the SC port is used for fiber optic transceivers, and the LC port is used for optical modules.
