It can forward electrical signals and provide exclusive electrical signal paths for any two network nodes connected to it, thereby avoiding transmission and port conflicts and improving broadband utilization efficiency.
From the perspective of the object of data forwarding, the router determines that the address for data forwarding uses the ID number of a different network, and the switch determines the address for forwarding data by using the MAC address or physical address.
From the working level, the router works based on IP addressing and works on the network layer of the OSI model, which can handle the TCP/IP protocol; the switch works on the relay layer based on MAC addressing.
From the perspective of application area, routers are mainly used to connect LANs and external networks, and switches are mainly used for data forwarding in LANs.
