News - China’s panel weights have surged. Will there be a top or two strong in the future?
China’s panel weights have surged. Will there be a top or two strong in the future?
After years of high investment and losses, China’s display panel industry has begun to reap the fruits: the global display panel production capacity is accelerating its transfer to China.
Global production capacity is concentrated in China, while Chinese production capacity is beginning to concentrate on BOE and other giants. In 2020, the two major mergers and acquisitions that have attracted much attention in the display panel industry are respectively led by BOE and China Star Optoelectronics.
The sudden new crown epidemic in 2020 has caused the global economy to press the pause button and cast a shadow over the display panel industry that has experienced the cold winter of nearly three years. However, since the second half of the year, the Korean production capacity has withdrawn and the epidemic has spawned remote homes.
From the perspective of inventory, the channel inventory in North America is basically empty, the channel inventory in Europe has entered a low level, and the channel inventory in mainland China is also slightly lower than the normal level. In order to cope with the traditional peak season of the spring market, brand manufacturers have strong demand for replenishment.
Manufacturers, their performance next year is highly anticipated. Many in the industry believe that in addition to factors such as home entertainment and remote office, the replacement wave brought by large-size HD TVs and 5G mobile phones will push the panel industry into a new upward cycle.
This is in stark contrast with the Chinese display panel giants that have continuously put into production and mergers in the counter-cyclical. Under the background of industry downturn and turmoil, BOE and China Star Optoelectronics, a subsidiary of TCL, have successively consolidated their leading positions in the display panel industry, especially in the LCD field, through massive investment and mergers and acquisitions.
Display panel companies look for new growth poles
. After gaining a foothold in the traditional display panel field, Chinese panel companies represented by BOE began to look for new growth poles.
The reporter noticed that since 2013, BOE has been seeking transformation. In that year, BOE established a smart system business group and built four major business systems including smart manufacturing, smart retail, smart car and smart energy.
According to IDC’s calculations, the domestic market in these fields will reach 500 billion US dollars in the next five years. In view of this, BOE will plan 10-15 innovation centers nationwide in the future, and focus on 6 market segments by building 5 platforms in the innovation centers.
