According to Sigmaintell’s consumer research on the PC user population, after the epidemic, the habits of Chinese digital users are changing, and the changes related to the habits of monitors are mainly reflected in the increase in demand for multi-screen interaction between monitors and laptops.
Before the epidemic, the proportion of direct interaction between monitors and notebooks of interviewed consumers was less than 20%, and after the epidemic rose to 31%. In overseas markets, more and more people interviewed said that they are increasingly using monitors as a secondary screen to directly connect to Chromebooks or laptops during home study and office work to improve user experience or relieve fatigue.
