It’s like, we have a red table in our house, you can see it and know it’s red when you turn on the light during the day or night. But if it’s night and the lights are turned off, can you still see it?
The first is that the brightness will be better than that of LCD illuminated by an external light source. The second and most important point is that since the pixels of the OLED screen are self-illuminating, and each pixel can freely control whether it emits light or not, when the OLED screen expresses the color of black, the pixels in the black part can not emit light at all.
Since the LCD itself does not emit light, even when it is black, the external light source will still illuminate the entire screen, and the black part is no exception, so the black will appear white. This feature makes OLED more power efficient when displaying black screens (especially for systems such as Windows Phone 7 where black is the dominant color).
