RESIDENTIAL ZONES PPCC has earmarked areas for the exclusive development of residential dwellings such as villas, twin villas, town houses, terrace houses and other residential uses.
Residential developments within the Phnom Penh City Center will be close to conveniences and yet far enough from the busy bustling Central Business District. These exclusively designed units will bring the latest residential concepts to Phnom Penh and will feature modern, efficient, environmentally friendly features and international grade architecture complete with lush landscapes.
Comprising 90 lavish villas, Residence 90 offers discerning homeowners the perfect combination of tranquility with urban convenience within an elite community of other like-minded individuals and families.
All ROVO units are designed with flexible-form of space for business operators who are free to set up the space according to own preferences. Be it a café, a restaurant, a start-up office, a bank, a boutique hotel, a meeting room or even a music studio, the option is limitless.
Roads leading up to the development are 30 meters wide with walkways emphasizing pedestrian friendliness, allowing shoppers to stroll around and revel in the Khmer inspired artwork, retail shops and green space. To ensure a refined touch to The Edge, all utility cables are designed and placed underground.
The Edge is a short stroll to many upcoming amenities including a shopping mall, F&B outlets, a night market, an international school, hotel, service apartments and offices. Yet, this exclusive freehold development integrates seamlessly with the greenery of Central Park, providing a perfect sanctuary away from the hustle and bustle of city life.
Enjoy first mover advantage to this superb development, The Edge.
These exclusively designed units are developed to bring in to Phnom Penh the latest in gated and guarded concepts, modern, efficient with environmentally friendly features and international grade architecture complete with lush landscapes.
Discover the Pearl of Cambodia and the vision behind its creation INVESTOR CENTER
Public areas in PPCC will feature lush greenery to complement the 22,000 sqm central park.
Recreational Rest and Relax in the Heart of the City
The center’s pedestrian green belt – sidewalks framed by lush greenery – will enable the community to enjoy leisure walks and hassle-free family days out at the 22,000 sqm central park, in addition to other recreational activities made available and accessible to all. Sports Complex
Infrastructure PPCC is an integrated township – unlike existing developments in Cambodia – and is focused on setting up comprehensive infrastructure systems.
Accessibility is also a key feature of PPCC. Set to ease the perennial traffic congestion and flooding issues Cambodia’s capital continues to face, the PPCC will be linked to the wider city through eight access points, resulting in a more fluid inner city system.
We’re opening our Careers Portal soon.
PLAY. A retail hub will be located within close proximity to residential developments in PPCC, and away from the high density Central Business District.
Strategically surrounded by city government departments and in close proximity to the Vattanac Capital Tower, Central Market, French Embassy and Calmette Hospital, this high density zone will be Phnom Penh’s first and only CBD. The CBD can be accessed from the south via the Russian Boulevard and from the east through Monivong Boulevard.
This design philosophy is infused throughout PPCC. It guides the development from conceptualization to design through to construction and beyond.
Sustainability: We think beyond the day a building is ready for occupants to ensure our projects are future-proofed with continued relevance and usefulness. We understand that cities grow and change and we seek to enable rather than impede this process by anticipating future infrastructure needs.
Since 2014, the PPCC has proactively adopted an innovative approach to community engagement and empowerment, recognizing the importance of inclusivity and giving back to the community.
