How can CBD be helpful in treating low back pain?
On the other hand, can cannabidiol (CBD) – the second most abundant cannabinoid produced by the cannabis plant – are an interesting product thanks to its ability to communicate with our bodies through numerous routes and the degree of safety in taking it. The World Health Organization recommends that CBD is safe and well tolerated by both adults and children.
The findings of this study CBD for low back pain treatment
Endocannabinoid receptors (CB1 and CB2) that have been found to work may play a role in important pain mediation processes and neuroinflammatory modulation. CBD may also affect certain central dopaminergic neuronal pain circuits and be involved in the activation of the serotonin and vanilloid receptor (TRPV1) – a complex mechanism likely responsible for diminishing pain control and, perhaps, the placebo effect (through anxiety reduction).
Anecdotal evidence also suggests that “CBD may reduce acute anxiety, impair the consolidation of anxiety-inducing memories, and facilitate the expulsion of previously acquired anxiety-related impressions.” These properties make the compound a promising compound for the treatment of anxiety, fear and pain-related conditions.
Overall, current research shows that patients report beneficial effects on chronic pain using CBD treatments, which the researchers suggest are likely due to the improvement in insomnia, anxiety, cognition and/or mood. While preliminary evidence from in vitro and animal studies suggests that CBD could be an important area of research for the treatment of low back pain in the future, further clinical evidence is needed to gain a clearer picture of the potential of this very interesting compound.
